---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy — MojiPond";
const description =
  "What MojiPond observes, stores, and sends while providing emoji autocomplete on macOS.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Your messages aren't sent to MojiPond.</h1>
    <div class="legal-note">
      <strong>No account. No app telemetry. No Messages database access.</strong
      >
      <p>Last updated August 1, 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What the Mac app observes</h2>
    <p>
      MojiPond receives global key events after you grant Input Monitoring.
      Unrelated keys are discarded immediately. After your configured trigger,
      the app holds a bounded shortcode candidate in memory long enough to
      search the local emoji catalog.
    </p>
    <p>
      Accessibility access lets MojiPond identify the focused editable control,
      read a limited token near the caret, place suggestions, and replace the
      token you chose. It refuses secure fields and unknown targets. MojiPond
      does not save raw keystrokes or message text.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
    <p>
      Imported packs, aliases, favorites, recent emoji, preferences, downloaded
      sticker artwork, and temporary media files live in the app's local
      containers. MojiPond does not offer an account or cloud sync.
    </p>

    <h2>When the app uses the network</h2>
    <p>Two optional features make HTTPS requests:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When online Noto search is enabled, MojiPond downloads Google's fixed
        emoji manifest, filters it on your Mac, and fetches only the artwork you
        choose. It doesn't send your search query.
      </li>
      <li>
        Signed update checks contact the configured update host after you
        request a check or enable automatic checks. Downloading an update
        remains a separate action.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Those hosts receive ordinary request metadata such as an IP address and
      user agent. MojiPond does not attach message contents, imported emoji,
      contact data, or a user account.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Event Posting</h2>
    <p>
      Image insertion in Messages may use Event Posting to issue a tagged paste
      command and, depending on your setting, Return. Unicode replacement does
      not need it when Accessibility can edit the target directly.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets no analytics cookies, runs no advertising scripts, and has
      no signup form. GitHub Pages hosts the files and may process normal HTTP
      request data under the
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        >GitHub Privacy Statement</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
